tests.question:
ABC Corporation is a domestic C corporation on a calendar year basis that has accumulated a net operating loss of $3,000,000.00 from tax years 2022 to 2024. On July 1, 2025 an investor group acquired 55.00% of ABC Corp's outstanding common stock from existing shareholders in one transaction. ABC Corp. has made the closing of the books election under Treas Reg §1.382-6(d) for the 2025 tax year.
The following has occurred before the acquisition:
The fair market value of all outstanding ABC Corp stock is $6,000,000.00;
Long term tax exempt rate for the month is 4.00%;
The fair market value of ABC Corp's assets is $4,800,000.00; and
The total adjusted basis of all ABC Corporation assets is $4,000,000.00.
During 2025:
Jan 1 to July 1 - taxable income of $150,000.00;
July 2 to Dec 31 - taxable income of $500,000.00;
Total taxable income before net operating loss is $650,000.00;
After the acquisition ABC Corp recognized $200,000.00 of gain on the sale of an investment property that is a recognized built-in gain under Internal Revenue Code §382(h)(2)(A).
Has an ownership change occurred, when, and under what guidance? What is ABC Corp’s annual limitation under Internal Revenue Code §382(b)(1) and what is their limitation applying the change year proportion rule under Internal Revenue Code §382(b)(3)? Does ABC Corp have a recognized net unrealized built in gain under Internal Revenue Code §382(h)(3)? If so, does the threshold apply and how does the $200,000.00 affect the tax §382 limitation for 2025? After the closing of the books election and all relevant limitations that can be applied, what is the maximum amount of the $3,000,000.00 net operating loss carryforward that ABC Corp may use in 2025, and what net operating loss carryforward balance remains for 2026, if any?
